# docs/ IS the published site root (GitHub Pages, goalworld.fun). Everything in this
# tree is world-readable unless listed here.
#
# Issue #881: internal working docs must never reach the deployed artifact.
# Consumed by:
#   scripts/pages/stage_public_tree.py   -> excludes these paths before upload
#   scripts/pages/guard_published_tree.py -> fails the deploy if one survives
# Entries ending in "/" mean a whole directory subtree; otherwise globs (fnmatch) match
# the relative path or the basename.
#
# Review before adding: an entry here hides a path from the public site. Deleting the
# files themselves is a separate, owner-approved decision (see
# docs/REPORTS/SECURITY_INTERNAL_DOCS_AUDIT_2026-09-10.md).

# --- Internal working docs: agent briefs, OA proposals, audits, scratch -------------
intake/
proposals/
REPORTS/
issues/
scratch/
hermes-workflow/
insights/
social/
x-reposts/
adr/
archive/
tests/
governance/
hackathons/
.wrangler/
.gitleaks.toml
.assetsignore

# --- Hard internal markers (any location) ------------------------------------------
*INTERNAL*
internal-*.md

# --- TIER B: internal ops docs that live in the docs/ root --------------------------
# Excluded from the deploy now (reversible, no file deleted). Repo removal / history
# purge needs owner confirmation: docs/REPORTS/SECURITY_INTERNAL_DOCS_AUDIT_2026-09-10.md
# NOTE: docs/publishing/ stays public for art/metadata, but the manuscript trees inside it
# (MANUSCRIPT/, EDICION_2026/, ENGLISH_EDITION_2026/) are excluded above — the reader page
# is built from them on the VPS and does not require them to be downloadable.
SECURITY_AUDIT.md
GROK_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md
IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md
GOALCHAIN_MASTER_PROMPTS_V1.md
EXECUTION_BACKLOG_90D.md
BACKLOG_STATUS_MODEL.md
AUDIT_STATE_2026-05-11.md
NFT_PROMPTS.md
PLAYER_IMAGE_PROMPTS.md
GOALCHAIN_PITCH_DECK.md

# --- Unpublished manuscript trees: commercial IP, must NEVER be published -----------
# The reader/sample pages (docs/go/reader/, docs/reader.html) are built FROM these files
# at deploy time on the VPS; the source manuscripts themselves do not need to be public.
# Adding an entry here hides the path from the site; it does not delete anything.
publishing/*/*/MANUSCRIPT/*
publishing/*/*/EDICION_2026/*
publishing/*/*/ENGLISH_EDITION_2026/*
publishing/*/*/OUTLINES/*
publishing/*/FILM/*
publishing/*/FILM
publishing/the_neural_wars_trilogy/00_SERIES_BIBLE_AND_CANON/*
publishing/the_neural_wars_trilogy/AI_AGENT_EDITORIAL_WORKBENCH/*
ceo-log.txt

